WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.150
Step six inspects what leaves.

2
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:06.166
Network and Transport owns the
agency's edge; inside Azure,

3
00:00:06.166 --> 00:00:11.187
Azure Firewall is the inspection point
for egress and east-west traffic.

4
00:00:11.187 --> 00:00:16.328
Learn's Zero Trust recommendations for
Azure Firewall check that outbound traffic

5
00:00:16.328 --> 00:00:20.954
routes through it, that threat intelligence
and intrusion detection are in

6
00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:25.213
alert and deny mode, that outbound T L
S is inspected, and that logs are on.

7
00:00:25.213 --> 00:00:28.710
Threat intelligence deny
needs Standard or Premium;

8
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.287
intrusion detection and T L
S inspection need Premium.

9
00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:34.767
Create a Premium policy in alert mode,

10
00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:40.126
add a default route from each workload
subnet to the firewall, and log everything.

11
00:00:40.126 --> 00:00:44.261
After two weeks of reading the
alerts, move to deny through a draft,

12
00:00:44.261 --> 00:00:47.325
so every change lands at
once and can be reviewed.

13
00:00:47.325 --> 00:00:51.605
Learn warns that deploying a draft
replaces the whole applied policy,

14
00:00:51.605 --> 00:00:54.187
so live edits made after
the draft are lost.

15
00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:58.346
T L S inspection needs a trusted
certificate authority in Key Vault,

16
00:00:58.346 --> 00:01:00.340
and spokes talk through the hub.
